<onlyinclude>'''Artificial life''' (ALife) is an interdisciplinary field that studies life-like organization, adaptation and evolution through constructed systems. These may be computer simulations, robots or engineered chemical and biological systems.

== Explanation ==
Rather than only observing existing organisms, researchers build simplified systems to investigate which mechanisms can produce features associated with life. A computer population may replicate and evolve, while a chemical model may explore how a self-maintaining boundary forms. Whether a particular artifact is itself alive depends on the definition and evidence.

